Standard aggressive Austrian 1901 opening to seize neutrals and position for Fall gains (SER via BUD, GRE via ALB, RUM/BUL via GAL pressure). F TRI - ALB uncontested (empty, agreed in plans with I/T), sets up GRE attack and eyes Adriatic stability with friendly Italy (VEN likely PIE/TYO, not south). A BUD - SER grabs key Balkan neutral safely (empty, shorter path than RUM, avoids bounce risk if Russia eyes RUM/UKR; Italy prefers this per diary vs Turkey Rum). A VIE - GAL pressures Russia (per contain goal/NAP test; empty now, likely WAR-Gal bounce ok as it signals strength without hitting homes; supports future RUM/UKR). No supports needed (all targets empty/uncontested). Avoids north/west (TYR/BOH) to not antagonize Germany/Italy. Tests trusts: Russia (no GAL retaliation hoped), Turkey (ALB blocks GRE vs their BUL?), Italy (SER mutual benefit). Positions for 2+ SC (SER + GRE/RUM) and 5-6 total by year-end. No holds, full aggression.

